The benchmark data in this directory is licensed under the Creative Commons Attribution 4.0
International licence (CC BY 4.0): https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/legalcode

This licence covers our own contributions: the Lean statements and proofs, the gold labels and
annotations, and the text we wrote or rewrote. The data also contains third-party material, which
stays under its authors' copyright and its own terms:

- excerpts of JMLR papers (Volume 18 onward) and of ICLR papers on OpenReview, all under CC BY 4.0.
  They are excerpts, converted from the published PDFs by OCR, with OCR damage repaired; ICLR
  excerpts have their equation and result numbers replaced by item-local ones;
- 4 JMLR papers before Volume 18, which state no public licence; their text is rewritten in our own
  words, with the mathematics unchanged;
- material from lecture notes and textbooks, each publicly available or used with the permission of
  its authors.

Per-source attribution (authors, copyright, licence, link and changes made) is in
`../ATTRIBUTION.json`. When redistributing an excerpt, carry its attribution with it.
